      "text": "#### Step 1: Determine the interval between replacements\nEach time Hal replaces the batteries, it is every 5 months.\n\n#### Step 2: Calculate the total number of intervals\nHe needs to replace them 25 times, so calculate the total intervals:\n\\[\n\\text{Total intervals} = 25 \\times 5 \\text{ months + 1}\n\\]\nEach interval is 5 months, and he replaces them 25 times, so we add 1 extra month:\n\\[\n\\text{Total intervals} = 25 \\times 5 + 1\n\\]\nMultiply 25 by 5:\n\\[\n25 \\times 5 = 125\n\\]\nAdd 1 more month:\n\\[\n125 + 1 = 126 \\text{ months}\n\\]\n\n#### Step 3: Match the total months to a calendar year\nWe need 126 months to determine the month. To convert this into years and months, divide the total months by 12:\n\\[\n\\frac{126}{12} = 10 \\text{ years and } 6 \\text{ months}\n\\]\nSo, the batteries will be replaced after 10 full years and 6 months.\n\n#### Step 4: Match the interval to the calendar year\nHal started the first replacement in May, so we start counting months from May. Every 12 months (one year), the batteries should be checked again. \n\nWe need to count the remainder (months beyond the last whole year):\n\\[\n6 \\text{ months from May}\n\\]\n\n#### Step 5: Count up from May to find the month\nMay + 6 months = \n\nStarting with May, we count:\n- June\n- July\n- August\n- September\n- October\n- November\n\nThus, after \\(\\boxed{\\text{November}}\\), the batteries will be changed the 25th time.",
