      "text": "Hal changes the batteries every 5 months. To find the month he will change the batteries for the 25th time, we start counting from May and add 5 months to May 24 times. This calculation leads us to October.\n\n\\[\n\\text{Month 1} = \\text{May} + 5 = \\text{October}\n\\] \n\\begin{align*}\n\\text{Month 2} &= \\text{October} + 5 \\\\\n&= 5 \\, \\text{months + 5 months} \\\\\n&= 10 \\, \\text{months + 5 months} \\\\\n&= 15 \\, \\text{months + 10% of 5 months} \\\\\n&= \\text{October} + 3 \\, \\text{months + 10% of 5} \\\\\n&= \\text{November}\n\\end{align*} \n\\begin{align*}\n\\text{Month 3} &= \\text{November} + 5 \\\\\n&= 10 \\, \\text{months + 5 months} \\\\\n&= 15 \\, \\text{months + 5 months} \\\\\n&= \\text{November} + 3 \\, \\text{months + 5 months} \\\\\n\\end{align*} \n\\begin{align*}\n&= \\text{December}\n\\end{align*} \n\\begin{align*}\n\\text{Month 4} &= \\text{December} + 5 \\\\\n&= 10 \\, \\text{months + 5 months} \\\\\n&= 15 \\, \\text{months + 5 months} \\\\\n&= 10 \\, \\text{months + 5 months} \\\\\n\\end{align*} \n\\begin{align*}\n&= \\text{January}\n\\end{align*} \n\\begin{align*}\n\\text{Month 5} &= \\text{January} + 5 \\\\\n\\end{align*} \n\\begin{align*}\n&= 10 \\, \\text{months + 5 months} \\\\\n&= 5 \\, \\text{months + 5 months} \\\\\n&= \\text{May}\n\\end{align*} \nIt becomes difficult to calculate manually, especially during final exams. We use a programming solution utilizing Python to solve the same.\n\\boxed{\\text{October}}\n\n\\begin{align*}\n\\text{Month 1} &= \\text{May} + 5 = \\text{October} \\\\\n\\text{Month 2} &= \\text{November} + 5 \\\\\n\\text{Month 3} &= \\text{December} + 5 \\\\\n\\text{Month 4} &= \\text{January} + 5 \\\\\n\\text{Month 5} &= \\text{May} + 5 \\\\\n&\\text{and so on}\n\\end{align*}",
